    <section class="section fade-up fade-up-2">
        <p>Parachute is open source. The most direct way to read about how it works is in the code itself &mdash; start with each repo's <code>README.md</code>. Below are the design notes that anchor architectural direction post-launch.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
        <h2>Architecture design notes</h2>
        <p>Capturing the shape Parachute is evolving toward.</p>
        <ul class="blog-list">
            <li>
                <a href="/design/2026-05-18-v06-deploy-architecture/" class="blog-post-card">
                    <h3>v0.6 deploy architecture &mdash; single Render container, hub-as-supervisor</h3>
                    <div class="date">2026-05-18</div>
                    <p class="excerpt">The self-host deploy shape locked in for v0.6: one container running hub-as-supervisor, vault / notes / scribe as child processes sharing a single persistent disk, modules installed at runtime via the admin SPA. The deploy mirror of the local model. Surfaced one-click at <a href="/deploy/render/">/deploy/render/</a>.</p>
                </a>
            </li>
            <li>
                <a href="https://github.com/ParachuteComputer/parachute.computer/blob/main/design/2026-04-20-module-architecture.md" class="blog-post-card" target="_blank">
                    <h3>Module architecture</h3>
                    <div class="date">2026-04-20</div>
                    <p class="excerpt">The canonical module protocol: <code>info</code>, <code>config</code>, <code>services.json</code>, <code>.well-known/parachute.json</code>. How Vault, Notes, Scribe, and third-party modules plug into a single ecosystem under one HTTPS URL.</p>
                </a>
            </li>
            <li>
                <a href="https://github.com/ParachuteComputer/parachute.computer/blob/main/design/2026-04-20-hub-as-portal-oauth-and-service-catalog.md" class="blog-post-card" target="_blank">
                    <h3>Hub as portal &mdash; OAuth and the service catalog</h3>
                    <div class="date">2026-04-20</div>
                    <p class="excerpt">OAuth architecture with the hub as issuer. One ecosystem sign-in, tokens carrying a service catalog, scopes that constrain what a client can reach.</p>
                </a>
            </li>
            <li>
                <a href="https://github.com/ParachuteComputer/parachute.computer/blob/main/design/2026-04-20-cloud-offering-sketch.md" class="blog-post-card" target="_blank">
                    <h3>Parachute Cloud &mdash; architecture sketch</h3>
                    <div class="date">2026-04-20</div>
                    <p class="excerpt">Cloud deployment shape: tenant-per-subdomain, Postgres-backed, CDN-hosted Notes, pooled Scribe. A plausible north star we refine when a first cloud user materializes. Note: this is the long-horizon hosted offering; v0.6 self-host (above) is the path shipping today.</p>
                </a>
            </li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
        <h2>Per-repo READMEs</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><a href="https://github.com/ParachuteComputer/parachute-hub" target="_blank"><strong>parachute-hub</strong></a> &mdash; the coordinator: <code>install</code>, <code>start</code>, <code>stop</code>, <code>expose</code>, and lifecycle for every module. OAuth issuer.</li>
            <li><a href="https://github.com/ParachuteComputer/parachute-vault" target="_blank"><strong>parachute-vault</strong></a> &mdash; the knowledge graph. REST + MCP, SQLite-backed. Portable-markdown export/import.</li>
            <li><a href="https://github.com/ParachuteComputer/parachute-notes" target="_blank"><strong>parachute-notes</strong></a> &mdash; browser-based companion for your vault. Installable multi-vault PWA.</li>
            <li><a href="https://github.com/ParachuteComputer/parachute-scribe" target="_blank"><strong>parachute-scribe</strong></a> &mdash; Whisper-compatible transcription API.</li>
            <li><a href="https://github.com/ParachuteComputer/parachute-agent" target="_blank"><strong>parachute-agent</strong></a> &mdash; a Parachute-flavored Claude Code distribution. Single binary, prewired.</li>
            <li><a href="https://github.com/ParachuteComputer/parachute-patterns" target="_blank"><strong>parachute-patterns</strong></a> &mdash; cross-repo conventions (naming, schemas, OAuth scopes, ports) and the <a href="https://github.com/ParachuteComputer/parachute-patterns/tree/main/cookbook" target="_blank">cookbook</a> of worked patterns.</li>
        </ul>
    </section>

